     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "I've logged the run as anomalous, most likely from a seal leak letting air into the tube. Exhaust O2 rose from about 3 to 33 ppm over the growth stage, well above the 2–6 ppm seen during the ramp. Pressure held at about 760 Torr, which argues against a blocked exhaust. Argon flow matched its setpoint, so a stuck flow controller is unlikely. Temperature and heater power were also steady.\n\nI recommended a test to confirm the leak before continuing. Either a leak check or a step up in argon flow would do: if O2 drops when flow increases, air is getting in. I had no normal-run reference values to compare against, and no characterization of the sample exists yet. Because oxygen was getting in during growth, whatever the sample shows later won't tell us much about the recipe itself."
     }
